      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LaCrosse%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "An accidental post office typo in 1889 kept the town unrecognized until 1896, despite always being called LaCrosse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lacrossecommunitypride.com/lacrosse-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Oregon Railroad and Navigation Company finished its line to LaCrosse in 1888, sparking a boom of hotels and stores.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LaCrosse%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2005 the La Crosse Arts and Beautification Council launched downtown renovations, promoting local culture and history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
